Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Tue Feb 4 13:53:35 2025 +0000
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Tue Feb 4 13:53:35 2025 +0000

    Bug 1936584 - Add former values to changed properties in the messages.onUpdated event. r=mkmelin


    This patch updates the messages.onUpdate event to include the former
    values, adding significant logic to retrieve the former values for
    `keywords` and `junkscore`.

    1. `keywords`:

    The currently used `nsIFolderListener.propertyFlagChanged` listener is
    intended to report changed flags instead of changed strings. The
    `nsIDBChangeListener.onHdrPropertyChanged` listener would be an option,
    but the API needs to listen to all folders, and it would not be feasible
    to register such a listener for all of them. This patch adds a new
    listener: `nsIMsgFolderNotificationService.msgPropertyChanged`.

    2. `junkscore`

    Junkscore handling is complex, because there is no central function to
    manipulate its value. Each implementation is directly acting on the
    database:
    - `nsMsgDBFolder::SetJunkScoreForMessages` : set junkscore with origin "filter"
    - `nsMsgDBView::ApplyCommandToIndices`: set junkscore with origin "user"
    - `onMessageClassified` listeners: set junkscore with origin "plugin"
    - `nsMsgDBFolder::CallFilterPlugins`: set junkscore with origin "whitelist"
    - `nsImapMailFolder::ApplyFilterHit`: set junkscore with origin "filter"
    - `nsImapMailFolder::HandleCustomFlags`: set junkscore with origin "imapflag" if unset

    See https://searchfox.org/comm-central/search?q=set.*%22junkscore%22&path=&case=false&regexp=true

    The current implementation is listening for the `msgsJunkStatusChanged`
    notification, which was only triggered in `ApplyCommandToIndices` via
    user changes in the UI. For now, I decided to limit the new notification
    to these UI events, and calls to `SetJunkScoreForMessages` (this is
    used by the filter service and users can apply filters after the
    message has been received/downloaded). From my current understanding,
    the other updates happen only through initial message parsing and do not
    need to be send as notifications to the API.

    What else ?

    I think at some point, we should add a central function to handle
    junkscore updates. For example `nsMsgDBFolder::SetJunkScoreForMessages`
    could get additional parameters to set `junkscoreorigin` and
    `junkpercent` as well. If so, I suggest to do it in a follow-up shortly,
    to not have to dig through the code again.

    Is this the best way to do it?

    I am not sure, if both properties should use a generic property
    notification, or a dedicated notification each. Assuming we introduce
    the central function to deal with junkscore updates, it could also be
    interesting to get a combined notification of `junkscore`, `junkorigin`
    and `junkpercent` - which would require a dedicated notification.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D235949

